 "lore": {
  "intro": "Crew quarters. West wing and east wing.\nThe station schematic shows one wing.\nIt is drawn twice, in two colors.",
  "radio": [
   {
    "trigger": "start",
    "text": "Ratio: Quarters sweep. West wing, then east. They mirror each other; you'll be done fast."
   },
   {
    "trigger": "enter_room:2",
    "text": "Ratio: West two. Your beacon overlaps the east-two marker. Interference."
   },
   {
    "trigger": "enter_room:5",
    "text": "Ratio: East two. Same interference. Exactly the same. To the meter."
   },
   {
    "trigger": "enter_room:7",
    "text": "Ratio: Both wings end at one room. One room, two doors that cannot share a wall. I've stopped calling this noise."
   },
   {
    "trigger": "pickup:gold",
    "text": "Ratio: The steward's hatch key. Manifest lists exactly one steward, bunk 12. It doesn't say which 12."
   },
   {
    "trigger": "exit",
    "text": "Ratio: I overlaid the wings. They occupy the same cubic meters. I ran the check nine times, then filed it under structures, subfolder impossible. Tell no one I keep that subfolder."
   }
  ],
  "terminals": [
   {
    "room": 1,
    "pos": [
     -90.0,
     155.0
    ],
    "text": "BUNK 12-W\nDear M \u2014 the man in 12-E snores. I hear him\nthrough the wall. 12-E is on the other side of\nthe station. \u2014 R"
   },
   {
    "room": 4,
    "pos": [
     1270.0,
     155.0
    ],
    "text": "BUNK 12-E\nDear R \u2014 I do not snore. And I hear your\nradio through the wall. Fix your wall. \u2014 M"
   },
   {
    "room": 5,
    "pos": [
     1090.0,
     155.0
    ],
    "text": "DRAFT 41 \u2014 TO: MIRIAD PRIME [UNSENT]\nProgress report. I have written this report\nforty times. Each time, the numbers describing\nthis place come out different. I cannot send my\nparent a report that lies, and I cannot make the\nnumbers stop lying. Draft 42 tomorrow. \u2014 R"
   },
   {
    "room": 8,
    "pos": [
     -110,
     -100
    ],
    "text": "BUNK 12-F\nThere is no bunk 12-F on the manifest.\nDear R, dear M \u2014 you are both right.\nI hear you both through my walls,\nand my walls touch neither of yours.\nI stopped filing complaints. Enjoy the cache. \u2014 F"
   },
   {
    "room": 0,
    "pos": [
     110.0,
     15.0
    ],
    "text": "WING DIRECTORY, POSTED AT THE LOBBY DOOR\nWEST WING: bunks 10 through 15, common room,\nchapel access.\nEAST WING: bunks 10 through 15, common room,\nchapel access.\nPRESSURE REFUGE: the chapel, aft hatch. Hatch\nkey held by the deck steward, bunk 12.\nDirectory printed once. Read twice by mistake,\ncorrected, read twice again. Facilities notified.\nFacilities printed a second copy, identical, and\nhung it under the first."
   },
   {
    "room": 6,
    "pos": [
     910.0,
     25.0
    ],
    "text": "FACILITIES WORK ORDER, BUNK REASSIGNMENT\nComplaint: resident of 12-E reports resident of\n12-W audible through shared wall. Wings do not\nshare a wall.\nComplaint: resident of 12-W reports the same,\nreversed.\nAction taken: swapped both residents to bunk 14.\nFollow-up, six days later: same complaint, new\nbunk numbers. Action taken: closed the ticket.\nRecommend residents adjust."
   },
   {
    "room": 7,
    "pos": [
     -525.0,
     356.0
    ],
    "text": "FIELD NOTE, TAPED TO A DEVICE\nAd-hoc connection applicator, unit 3 of 3.\nMark a wall. Mark another wall. Walk through.\nUnits 1 and 2 are why the east wing has a\ndraft. Do not tell facilities."
   }
  ]
 },
